# BuildKit reads `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` in preference to the context's
# `.dockerignore`, so the production base-image build can exclude the multi-GB host
# `target/` without adding an ignore file to the repo root. The build needs the
# Cargo workspace and nothing else.
target/
**/node_modules/
.git/
packages/
docs/
deploy/
e2e/
**/dist/
**/.wrangler/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/
